{"id":"397271029","kind":"article","title":"学习别人的间隔重复记忆卡片通常是无效的","author":"Andy Matuschak","original_authors":["Andy Matuschak"],"original_source_urls":["https://notes.andymatuschak.org/z38fLX4H8oq9eXKnZH7wk8qDXfBLg2bxVyA2M","https://notes.andymatuschak.org/zAPNwLWboaoymgEAPyUwjnT"],"publisher":"Thoughts Memo","column":"间隔重复 & 注意力管理","date":"2021-08-07","updated":"2026-10-27","votes":22,"comment_count":2,"minutes":1,"chars":542,"keywords":["间隔重复","检索练习","助记媒介","学习材料设计","Anki"],"summary":"文章主张，若尚未掌握某主题，先读教科书再做间隔重复卡片，比直接背诵他人牌组更合适，因为卡片本身难以承载完整讲解，而且现成牌组质量常不理想。作者以“先学再记”和卡片作为交流媒介的局限为由，提醒读者不要把 SRS 牌组当作独立教材。","zhihu_url":"https://zhuanlan.zhihu.com/p/397271029","restoration":null,"toc":[{"id":"sec-1","level":2,"title":"链接至本文（已汉化）"},{"id":"sec-2","level":2,"title":"声明"}],"html":"<p data-pid=\"m8cKPT2F\">一旦理解了<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/z4bR1HVvDUhMXDm5SJB4Tiw4xGbrm9AfXWgbc\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">间隔重复记忆系统使记忆成为一种选择</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-1\"><a href=\"#ref-1\">[1]</a></sup>和<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/z8VFVdTR19snWjFMxnyNabBCbmeoWrQ287TdT\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">学习越来越复杂的想法可能相当于形成更大的有效组块</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-2\"><a href=\"#ref-2\">[2]</a></sup>，那么通过下载别人的<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/z4eXdSMJFv2qVGXSUEKH4vdcHBrLHcFY1ZGfC\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">间隔重复记忆系统</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-3\"><a href=\"#ref-3\">[3]</a></sup>牌组来吞噬新知识是非常诱人的。但是，假设你之前从未学习过相关知识，你阅读教科书中关于细胞生物学的章节要比你背诵别人的牌组好得多：你必须<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/z2gsbsviCdBJbefxvenDcvYbYDgssBZHdgd9\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">先学再记</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-4\"><a href=\"#ref-4\">[4]</a></sup>。同时，<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/z1YhDPWyvzzkC79LFcF4DSTanKpEGpic8bAe\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">单独的间隔重复记忆卡片是一种糟糕的交流媒介</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-5\"><a href=\"#ref-5\">[5]</a></sup>；你仍然需要教科书的叙述</p><p data-pid=\"PZZjnTUs\">另外，大多数可下载的 SRS 牌组都做得很差：<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/z3ntJ7w9C3uapYp1m3gy2EK6PN788guzEoUNN\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">写好间隔重复记忆卡片很难</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-6\"><a href=\"#ref-6\">[6]</a></sup>。</p><p data-pid=\"UCcsOYzh\">另请参阅：<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/z4rRX3qwSSJRsEkdXKwH2shamgHNeRthrMLiF\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">助记媒介</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-7\"><a href=\"#ref-7\">[7]</a></sup>，它试图解决这个问题。</p><p data-pid=\"BXJ0nESp\">有关笔记：<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/z219EBYg9SbQzF372qudzgJpArt4Bmfhrczkg\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">亲自写间隔重复卡片似乎能促进理解</a></p><h2 id=\"sec-1\">链接至本文（已汉化）</h2><ul><li data-pid=\"UfGx3pFE\"><a class=\"internal tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"399738674\" href=\"#/post/399738674\">间隔重复系统能力的限制因素是写出足够多的好卡片</a></li><li data-pid=\"lHODqH6n\"><a class=\"internal tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"396775375\" href=\"#/post/396775375\">单独的间隔重复记忆卡片是一种糟糕的交流媒介</a></li><li data-pid=\"dgQmlrQG\"><a class=\"internal tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"694032460\" href=\"#/post/694032460\">用间隔重复系统来看穿数学概念 - Michael Nielsen</a></li><li data-pid=\"BmLUPNs1\"><a class=\"internal tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"719498216\" href=\"#/post/719498216\">程序教学</a></li></ul><h2 id=\"sec-2\">声明</h2><p data-pid=\"WuHyDe9U\">此内容发布由 Andy Matuschak 许可。未经允许，不得转载或修改。保留所有权利。</p><blockquote data-pid=\"Yh58DDq2\"><a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"http://paratranz.cn/projects/3131\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Thoughts Memo</a> 汉化组译制<br/>原文：<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/z38fLX4H8oq9eXKnZH7wk8qDXfBLg2bxVyA2M\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Studying another person’s spaced repetition memory prompts is usually ineffective</a></blockquote><hr/><ol class=\"references\"><li id=\"ref-1\"><a aria-label=\"返回正文\" class=\"ref-back\" href=\"#cite-1\">↩</a> 间隔重复记忆系统使记忆成为一种选择 <a class=\"tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"397582470\" href=\"#/post/397582470\">站内阅读 ↗</a></li><li id=\"ref-2\"><a aria-label=\"返回正文\" class=\"ref-back\" href=\"#cite-2\">↩</a> 学习越来越复杂的概念可能相当于形成更大的有效组块 <a class=\"tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"402333898\" href=\"#/post/402333898\">站内阅读 ↗</a></li><li id=\"ref-3\"><a aria-label=\"返回正文\" class=\"ref-back\" href=\"#cite-3\">↩</a> 间隔重复记忆系统（Spaced repetition memory system） <a class=\"tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"404257681\" href=\"#/post/404257681\">站内阅读 ↗</a></li><li id=\"ref-4\"><a aria-label=\"返回正文\" class=\"ref-back\" href=\"#cite-4\">↩</a> 先学再记 <a class=\"tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"550695797\" href=\"#/post/550695797\">站内阅读 ↗</a></li><li id=\"ref-5\"><a aria-label=\"返回正文\" class=\"ref-back\" href=\"#cite-5\">↩</a> 单独的间隔重复记忆卡片是一种糟糕的交流媒介 <a class=\"tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"396775375\" href=\"#/post/396775375\">站内阅读 ↗</a></li><li id=\"ref-6\"><a aria-label=\"返回正文\" class=\"ref-back\" href=\"#cite-6\">↩</a> 写好间隔重复记忆卡片很难 <a class=\"tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"397245681\" href=\"#/post/397245681\">站内阅读 ↗</a></li><li id=\"ref-7\"><a aria-label=\"返回正文\" class=\"ref-back\" href=\"#cite-7\">↩</a> 助记媒介 <a class=\"tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"459483765\" href=\"#/post/459483765\">站内阅读 ↗</a></li></ol>","rec_chain":[{"id":"397245681","title":"写好间隔重复记忆卡片很难","author":"Andy Matuschak","votes":19,"minutes":2,"reason":"同专栏上一篇 · 间隔重复 & 注意力管理"},{"id":"397582470","title":"间隔重复记忆系统使记忆成为一种选择","author":"Andy Matuschak","votes":19,"minutes":2,"reason":"同专栏下一篇 · 间隔重复 & 注意力管理"},{"id":"550695797","title":"先学再记","author":"Andy Matuschak","votes":18,"minutes":1,"reason":"本文直接引用"},{"id":"459483765","title":"助记媒介（Mnemonic medium）","author":"Andy Matuschak","votes":37,"minutes":6,"reason":"本文直接引用"},{"id":"396775375","title":"单独的间隔重复记忆卡片是一种糟糕的交流媒介","author":"Andy Matuschak","votes":13,"minutes":1,"reason":"本文直接引用"}],"rec_bridge":[{"id":"594372725","title":"用间隔重复软件记住一门编程语言","author":"Derek Sivers","votes":230,"minutes":8,"reason":"跨作者共鸣「检索练习」· Derek Sivers"},{"id":"412012134","title":"JAnki：写给程序员们的 13 条 Anki 使用经验","author":"Jack Kinsella","votes":148,"minutes":10,"reason":"跨作者共鸣「检索练习」· Jack Kinsella"}],"rec_answers":[{"id":"2193593015","title":"从Anki过渡到Supermemo需要注意些什么呢？","author":"Thoughts Memo","votes":110,"minutes":4,"reason":"核心节选引用 · 110 赞同","evidence":"正文链接锚文本明确指向该译文标题或具体关键词。"},{"id":"2045404097","title":"想问各位知友，用anki买别人做好的卡牌资源OK吗，还是自己做比较好，但感觉自己做要耗费很多时间呀？","author":"Thoughts Memo","votes":65,"minutes":1,"reason":"观点化用 · 65 赞同","evidence":"回答说数学、计算机和物理等知识不宜轻易用他人牌组，并补充现成牌组质量难评估；目标译文明确建议先学再记、认为卡片单独作为教材不佳且可下载牌组多质量差，属于该观点的压缩改述。"}]}